url: https://www.interface.com/US/en-US/sustainability/our-history

Carpet tile company founded by [[Ray Anderson]].

After 1994 it set itself "Mission Zero": no waste, no impact, no footprint by 2020. It takes its own carpet tiles back to make new ones, which makes it a large, working [[Technical Nutrient]] loop run by one company.

The top-down counterpart to the [[Oka Chair]], which builds its loop from farms and a makerspace.

See [[Circular Economy Companies]], [[Scaling Out]]

Sources:

* [[Interface: 30+ Years of Sustainability|https://www.interface.com/US/en-US/sustainability/our-history]]
* [[It's Easy Being Green: The Legacy of Ray Anderson (Center for American Progress)|https://www.americanprogress.org/article/its-easy-being-green-the-legacy-of-ray-anderson/]]
